=== Contributing to a Project
tag::concept[]

Now that Nora and Sam have their accounts, let's walk through how they actually use GitHub to collaborate. While they both have push access to the main `sketchspark` repo, they follow a process called the **GitHub Flow** to ensure all design changes are reviewed before being finalized.

==== Forking Projects
tag::concept[]

(((forking)))
As we mentioned in Chapter 5, external contributors like Marcus use **forking**. When Marcus "forks" the SketchSpark project, GitHub creates an identical copy of Nora's repo under Marcus's own namespace (`marcus-design/sketchspark`).

To fork, Marcus simply clicks the **Fork** button at the top-right of Nora's project page.

.The Fork button: creating your own sandbox
image::images/forkbutton.png[The Fork button]

Now Marcus has a writable copy where he can experiment with new icon styles. When he's ready, he will contribute those changes back to Nora via a **Pull Request**.

[[ch06-github_flow]]
==== The GitHub Flow
tag::concept[]

(((GitHub, Flow)))
The "GitHub Flow" is the team's standard operating procedure. It’s built around short-lived branches and collaborative review.

1.  **Branch:** Sam creates a branch for his work (e.g., `option/card-layout`).
2.  **Commit:** He commits his exports and notes locally.
3.  **Push:** He pushes the branch to GitHub.
4.  **Pull Request:** Sam opens a Pull Request (PR) to start a discussion.
5.  **Review:** Nora reviews the UI and leaves comments.
6.  **Merge:** Once approved, Nora merges the PR into `main`.

==== Opening a Pull Request
tag::walkthrough[]

(((Pull Requests, opening)))
After Sam pushes his `option/card-layout` branch, he visits the GitHub repository page. GitHub notices the new branch and shows a "Compare & pull request" button.

When Sam clicks it, he's presented with a form. He gives the PR a title—`[Design: Results] Prototype new card-based grid`—and describes his goals.

.Opening a Pull Request for design review
image::images/blink-03-pull-request-open.png[Opening a PR]

==== Reviewing and Discussing Changes
tag::walkthrough[]

(((Pull Requests, reviews)))
Once the PR is open, it becomes a **collaborative space**. Nora receives a notification and clicks in to see Sam's work.

GitHub provides a "Files changed" tab where Nora can see the diff. For text files like `design-tokens.json`, she sees a line-by-line comparison. For PNGs, GitHub provides a visual diff tool that allows her to slide between the "Before" and "After" versions of the layout.

Nora can click on any line or any part of an image to leave a comment: "I love the rounded corners here, but let's check the contrast on the secondary text."

.Conversational feedback on a PR
image::images/blink-04-pr-comment.png[PR Comment]

==== Merging the Pull Request
tag::procedure[]

(((Pull Requests, merging)))
After a few rounds of feedback and minor tweaks from Sam, Nora is happy with the result. She clicks the big green **Merge pull request** button.

Sam’s work is now integrated into the `main` branch. GitHub automatically closes the PR and Nora deletes the `option/card-layout` branch from the server to keep things tidy.
